# Copy to .env. Everything here is OPTIONAL — the engine builds books with none of it.
# Only image generation and LLM drafting read this file.
# The cockpit's keys tab overrides any of this, for the one request that needs it.

# The default image provider is `agy`: the Antigravity CLI, signed into your Google
# account. No API key, no per-image charge. Install it, run `agy` once to log in, then
# `node engine/tools/gen-image.mjs --check`.

# Where the agy binary is, if it is not on your PATH.
# AGY_BIN=C:\Users\you\AppData\Local\agy\bin\agy.exe

# The model that DRIVES the CLI (not the image model). The CLI retires these, so if
# --check says the default is gone, run `agy models` and put a listed one here.
# AGY_DRIVER_MODEL=gemini-3.8-flash-medium

# Fallback provider: the Gemini image API, which is metered and needs a key from
# https://aistudio.google.com/apikey. Only used with `--provider gemini`.
# GEMINI_API_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DRAFTING (optional)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# `draft-block.mjs` and the cockpit's draft panel need a model. Without a key
# here they still work against Ollama or LM Studio, which run on your machine
# and cost nothing. That is the recommended starting point.
#
# Run `node engine/tools/llm.mjs --list` to see every provider, whether it is
# configured on this machine, and what it costs.

# --- local, free, no key, no quota, no data leaving the machine -------------
# Install Ollama (https://ollama.com) then `ollama pull qwen2.5:7b`.
# OLLAMA_MODEL=qwen2.5:7b
# LM Studio exposes the same API on this port when its local server is running.
# LMSTUDIO_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:1234/v1

# --- free tier, needs a key, quota can be cut off at any time ---------------
# GEMINI_API_KEY=          # https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=      # https://openrouter.ai/keys
# GROQ_API_KEY=            # https://console.groq.com/keys
# GITHUB_TOKEN=            # https://github.com/settings/tokens  (needs "models" scope or Copilot Pro)
# MISTRAL_API_KEY=         # https://console.mistral.ai

# --- paid. Never called without --allow-paid --------------------------------
# OPENAI_API_KEY=          # https://platform.openai.com/api-keys
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=       # https://console.anthropic.com/settings/keys
# XAI_API_KEY=             # https://console.x.ai
#
# These three bill per token on every call. The tools refuse them unless you
# pass --allow-paid, and nothing auto-selects them. That gate is deliberate:
# a tool that quietly spends your money is a tool you stop running.

# Override any provider's endpoint or model without editing the tools, which is
# what you want when a provider renames a model or you front it with a proxy.
# OLLAMA_BASE_URL=
# GEMINI_BASE_URL=
# GEMINI_MODEL=
# OPENAI_BASE_URL=
# OPENAI_MODEL=
# ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL=
# ANTHROPIC_MODEL=
# XAI_BASE_URL=
# XAI_MODEL=
